  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 108 AM Saturday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Seasonal temperatures and pleasant conditions \nthrough the weekend. Temperatures will gradually trend above normal \ntowards the middle to latter part of next week.\n\nAn early season Nor'easter will affect portions of the northern Mid-\nAtlantic and southeastern New England this weekend will linger over \nthat region into early next week. The system will eventually weaken \nand get kicked eastward as mid/upper level ridging develops over the \ncentral and southern US and tracks eastward into the Carolinas \nduring the middle to latter part of next week.\n\nExpect a very pleasant and mainly clear/sunny weekend with highs \ntoday in the mid 70s to around 80. Highs will slowly moderate into \nthe lower 80s Sunday and Monday. Lows will continue very cool, with \n40s over the Piedmont again tonight and lower to mid 50s elsewhere, \nmoderating into the 50s early in the week. \n\nWe can expect a warming trend toward the middle to latter part of \nnext week as ridging builds in from the west. Rising thicknesses and \nheights will favor a trend to above normal highs in the mid to upper \n80s Wednesday through Friday. Lows will return to the 60s. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Dry weather overall, with a signal for increased \nrain chances very late next week or weekend.\n\nIt looks dry most, if not all this week. A mid/upper level high \npressure will build east from the Plains to over our region late \nthis week. This will keep it dry and warm this week. \n\nOur best chance of a return to unsettled weather may not come until \nSaturday as high pressure shifts offshore and a progressive trough \nmoves into the central U.S. by Fri-Sat. This should signal a pattern \nchange with the trough to our west by next weekend and a return SW \nflow with increasing moisture from the Gulf.",
